  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Envisioning Vivid Red**\n\nI\'m now picturing the canvas particles. They\'re no longer faint; I\'m going for bright, glowing, vibrant red Perlin noise structures that stand out on a black background. The red value will be high, between 220 and 255. The greens and blues, however, need adjustment.\n\n\n**Refining Background Color**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the background. The WebGL fragment shader will output pure black, or an extremely low ambient dark burgundy. I\'ve adjusted the code for `blueVal` for a truly neon red glow and have changed the alpha and particle count to allow filaments to flow beautifully. Now I need to check `PhoenixParticles.tsx` and work on the phoenix bird shape that is similar to the hunger games logo. I\'m also looking at the flower from the inspiration website.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Black Canvas**\n\nI\'m now integrating interactivity into the black background canvas. The goal is to ensure the glowing red Perlin noise trails respond directly to user interaction. I\'ll need to focus on how the phoenix bird particles interact with the user, and make it larger within the threejs code. This includes ensuring interactive elements don\'t overlap with static text, and ensuring round corner images are smaller.\n\n\n**Enhancing Fiery Trails**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the trails. I want them to resemble glowing firefly traces on the black field. I\'m increasing the canvas particle flow speed to achieve this effect. I\'m aiming for beautiful, glowing light-traces and will be experimenting to achieve the perfect opacity of the red strokes.\n\n**Crafting Mockingjay Phoenix**\n\nI\'m working on the Mockingjay-inspired phoenix bird particle system. I need to figure out how to recreate the Hunger Games logo. I\'m planning a thick, fiery ring of sparks to enclose a stylized bird shape with upward-stretching wings. The goal is a majestic bird structure inside a circle. I\'ll need to develop the ring structure with the right radius, random angular distribution, twisting and curling.\n\n\n**Implementing Interactive Emblems**\n\nI\'m now integrating mouse interaction to warp and swirl the particles, inspired by the Lewiszhang.dev rose, with attraction and repulsion. I\'m focusing on creating a majestic, recognizable emblem shape with the Hunger Games bird within a circle, mathematically defined in `PhoenixParticles.tsx`. The goal is to make the phoenix large, centered, and premium-looking, blending seamlessly with the page. I\'m also addressing the issue of interaction over absolute text overlays.\n\n\n**Addressing Mouse Interaction**\n\nI\'m now focusing on ensuring that the interactive background responds to mouse movements, even over text elements. I\'ve confirmed window-level mouse move listeners are active in both `VectorNoiseCanvas.tsx` and `PhoenixParticles.tsx`. I\'m double-checking for any `pointer-events` conflicts in `App.tsx` and text blocks. The plan is to extend interactivity to the title and text paragraphs, and ensure the background is interactive when hovering over the titles and text paragraphs as well.\n\n**Styling Carousel Images**\n\nNow, I\'m adjusting image styling and layout. The goal is to make the images smaller and more visually cohesive with the new Three.js particle design. I\'m modifying the marquee image container in `App.tsx` by reducing its height and moving it further down the page. I\'m also ensuring the images themselves have highly rounded corners.\n\n\n"
