    thinking: "**Analyzing Bird Shape**\n\nI\'m currently focused on reshaping the phoenix bird to more closely resemble bird wings, aiming for a larger form. The geometry attributes are currently generated within a loop iterating through a particle count of 28,000. My immediate task is to analyze this generation process to optimize and refine the bird\'s shape based on wing aesthetics.\n\n\n**Refining Wing Geometry**\n\nI\'m now diving into the precise calculations for feather fanning angles. I\'m focusing on ensuring feathers radiate correctly, down and out on the outer wing and back and out on the inner wing. This should allow beautiful feather posturing and contribute to a more aesthetically pleasing wing structure. I\'m aiming for a natural, clean look.\n\n\n**Scaling Wing Bones**\n\nI\'m now scaling the wing base bone for a wider wingspan, directly impacting the overall size. I\'m adjusting the `wingX` calculation to increase the wing\'s breadth. Simultaneously, I\'m reevaluating the feather length calculation to ensure the feathers extend proportionately. I want the wings to be noticeably larger and more visually striking.\n\n\n**Adjusting Wing Spread**\n\nI\'m now focusing on increasing the size and density of the wing feathers. I\'ve adjusted the calculation of wingX and wingY coefficients to create a more majestic \"V\" shape with the wing bones. I increased wingX from 1.25 to 1.65, and wingY from 1.22 to 1.55. Also, the feather fan angle is adjusted to accommodate these changes. I\'m aiming for pronounced feather size to fill the wings more completely.\n\n\n**Expanding Feather Length**\n\nI\'ve increased the feather length multiplier, expecting significantly larger wings and a more impressive visual. To maintain balanced proportions, I\'m now scaling the body and tail. I am modifying the torso, neck, head, and tail parameters to match the larger wings. I\'m choosing to model everything natively for better detail.\n\n\n**Sizing Up The Bird**\n\nI\'m now focusing on making the bird larger, aiming for a dramatic impact within the hero text backdrop. I\'ll need to edit `PhoenixParticles.tsx` to expand the wingspan and feather shapes. I\'m focusing on lines 47-131 of `/src/components/PhoenixParticles.tsx`, as they control the body, head, and tail. My intent is to adjust the body geometry to achieve the desired larger scale.\n\n\n**Modeling Neck and Head**\n\nI\'m now focusing on lines 16-46 in `/src/components/PhoenixParticles.tsx`. I am analyzing the neck and head geometry for optimal bird proportions. I\'m focusing on the slender neck and sharp head, and I\'ll carefully adjust the parameters to create a more majestic and balanced silhouette. I will ensure a smooth transition from the body to the head.\n\n\n**Adjusting Wing Feathers**\n\nI\'m now implementing the sleek, outspread reference image to refine the wings. I\'m focusing on the feather generation, specifically the 16 distinct feathers per wing. I\'m aiming for clean posturing with feather fanning angle calculations to achieve beautiful outward radiation. I\'ve adjusted featherLength for a tapering profile, and I\'m currently using a featherID and u to control feather position.\n\n\n**Refining Tail Feathering**\n\nI\'m now implementing the cascading longsword tail feather design. I\'ve focused on the 7 distinct ribbon-like strands, controlling their fanning and swooping effects. I\'m using random values to determine feather length and ensuring symmetrical x offsets. Now, I\'m working to make them beautiful!\n\n\n**Optimizing Wing Feathers**\n\nI\'m now implementing layered wing feathers to enhance detail, striving for a majestic phoenix look. I\'m focusing on refining feather fanning angles for distinct outer, mid, and inner layers. The goal is to achieve an elegant upward curve in the wing bones, complemented by feathers that sweep backward and outward, creating a soaring appearance. I\'m reviewing the wing bone calculations.\n\n\n**Calculating Feather Angles**\n\nI\'m now diving into optimizing feather angles, especially focusing on `featherID` and `u` values. I am analyzing how these variables impact the `featherLength` and the resulting wing aesthetics. I\'m focusing on ensuring feathers radiate correctly. The goal is a more elegant and realistic wing structure with a hand-drawn look. I\'ve broken down the calculations and I\'m verifying the shapes.\n\n\n"
